 $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{x=-1,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183448" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e0b252f-632c-5fb4-955e-f2c2686886d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421142 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{implies}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{if}\\,{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{only if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $P⇔Q$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $P:$ $A$ triangle is right.\n\n- $Q:$ $A$ triangle has two complementary angles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "204c3d5d-7433-5e9d-bacd-9011685dc6a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421143 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the correct grammatical construction of $P⇔Q$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ A triangle is right **if and only if** it has two complementary angles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ as a sentence given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c8d7440-4eac-56af-a31b-85c3ab92c898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421144 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following grammatica