 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421155 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is **NOT** a grammatical construction for the biconditional $P⇔Q?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421155 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f00a0a1e-c589-5b06-8786-738dfcf01ab1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421155 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that is NOT a grammatical construction for $P⇔Q$ is \"If $P,$ then $Q$\" (this is the grammatical construction of $P⇒Q).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
